QuantPy Control Panel - local setup
===================================
(See README.md for the full guide.)

1. Install
   python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate     # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
   pip install -e ".[bot]"

2. Configure
   cp .env.example .env     # fill in keys, QUANT_USER, SECRET_KEY, password (hash)
   Keep ALPACA_BASE_URL=https://paper-api.alpaca.markets (paper trading).
   NEVER commit .env.

3. 2FA (mandatory)
   python setup_2fa.py      # scan the QR code from .secrets/, enter the 6-digit code

4. Start
   python server.py         # http://127.0.0.1:5000
   Log in -> enter the TOTP code -> accept the risk notice -> Run Once / Start Bot.

5. Tests
   pip install -e ".[dev]" && pytest

Safety: paper trading is the default; live trading needs three explicit opt-ins
(docs/LEGAL_DE.md). The kill switch and audit log live in ./audit (back it up).
